#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:5
#: c5ea7eff91a442fd971ba9aaa66c6efc
msgid "3DR Solo - Smart Battery Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:7
#: ab7c1d57deba4d72bf9ed229b6a7f95a
msgid "The Solo Smart Battery may need recalibration from time to time.  The following write up details how execute a recalibration of the BMS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:10
#: 46455fcec1b042b6a5ee8c8166e13514
msgid "Gently discharge the battery pack until it cuts off the first time (this is around 12V)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:11
#: e7a9d2bad23e4f85888d39c536e1bfaf
msgid "Allow the pack the relax for at least 5 hours.  The pack's voltage will climb above 12V during this process.  **DO NOT TRY TO DISCHARGE THE PACK AGAIN.**  Damage to the battery may result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:12
#: fda3f20ed6514401abd3285e812cf5fa
msgid "Charge the pack completely and leave it on the charger for 48 hours.  The pack will relax, then do a balance cycle, then top off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:13
#: d88a0ec46efa4bdb969651be09a99963
msgid "Let the pack sit for at least 2 hours off the charger before using the pack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/solo_battery_calibration.rst:15
#: 933884890a7d43e2b02d3ee9557eb1c7
msgid "This tutorial was written by the Solo EE team (Jeff Wurzbach and Philip Rowse)."
msgstr ""
